  "notes": [
    "Regular -AR verb — follows standard -AR endings with no exceptions",
    "Past participle: *interesado* (regular; also used as an adjective meaning \"interested\" or, negatively, \"self-interested\")",
    "**Special usage**: like *gustar*, *interesar* is most often used with an indirect object pronoun + 3rd-person verb form, where the Spanish subject is the thing that \"interests,\" not the person: *me interesa la historia* (I'm interested in history — literally \"history interests me\"), *me interesan las ciencias* (I'm interested in the sciences)",
    "Indirect object pronouns: me, te, le, nos, les",
    "Related verbs with the same construction: *gustar* (to like), *encantar* (to love), *molestar* (to bother)",
    "Related words: *interés* (interest, noun), *interesante* (interesting), *interesado/a* (interested; or self-interested/scheming, depending on context)"
  ],
